If you're really just looking for the logical meaning, it's ganai and ganai
only. {go} would imply some sort of check on the thing coming up afterward,
which doesn't make sense.

As for elseif blocks, you could perhaps do this with {cei}?:
ganai ... cei broda gi brode
ga broda gi'enai brodi cei broda gi brodo
etc. Ugly though.

